# tests/deep-deps, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): running this test is
# evaluating this directory.
#
# A CLIENT TEST — it drives `caos-cli`, so its base is `DEEP-DEPS/lib`
# (tests/lib), the image that stages a git worktree and then runs `worker1`.
# DEPping on `lib` is the greppable marker of which tests are client tests.
#
#   --test  this directory itself, staged into the repo as ./test with its
#           DEEP-DEPS alongside. `--test:@=.` is inert by construction:
#           `strip_caos_expr` removes this file from the tree before the
#           expression is evaluated against it, so nothing recurses.
#   --cli   the client under test; --salt is what makes --test-salt re-run this
run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/lib --worker1:@=worker.sh --test:@=. --cli:@=cli --salt:@=salt
